<div data-type="1" data-title-level="2" class="oc-wysiwyg-container">
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel">
<h2>Latest News</h2>
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel-content">
<p><div class="oc-quick-list oc-quick-list-grid oc-quick-list-grid-1 landing-page-list-container clearfix"><div class="grid" role="list"><div class="col-xs-12 col-m-4" role="listitem">
	<div class="list-item-container" >		
		<article>
			<a href="https://www.denvergov.org/Government/Agencies-Departments-Offices/Agencies-Departments-Offices-Directory/Denver-Clerk-and-Recorder/About-the-Denver-Clerk-and-Recorder/Comms-and-Community-Engagement/media-releases/2026/10.14-FEF-Distribution"   target="">
				<H2 class="list-item-title">
					Five Receive Final FEF Payment for 2026 City Council Vacancy Election
				</H2>
				<p>		
					The Denver Clerk and Recorder has authorized an additional $273,888.09 in Fair Elections Fund disbursements to five eligible candidates running in the 2026 City Council At-Large Seat B vacancy election.
				</p>
			</a>
		</article>
	</div>
</div><div class="col-xs-12 col-m-4" role="listitem">
	<div class="list-item-container" >		
		<article>
			<a href="https://www.denvergov.org/Government/Agencies-Departments-Offices/Agencies-Departments-Offices-Directory/Denver-Clerk-and-Recorder/About-the-Denver-Clerk-and-Recorder/Comms-and-Community-Engagement/media-releases/2026/9.17-Vacancy-Election-Disbursement-One"   target="">
				<H2 class="list-item-title">
					Five Candidates Receive FEF Disbursements for 2026 Vacancy Election
				</H2>
				<p>		
					The Denver Clerk & Recorder has authorized $180,189.00 in Fair Elections Fund disbursements to five eligible candidates running in the 2026 City Council At-Large Seat B vacancy election. This is the first disbursement for the 2026 vacancy election and matches eligible contributions received between Aug. 5, 2026 and Aug. 31, 2026.
				</p>
			</a>
		</article>
	</div>
</div><div class="col-xs-12 col-m-4" role="listitem">
	<div class="list-item-container" >		
		<article>
